  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4103.56 Low vapor pressure VOC (LVP-VOC)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4103.56 “Low vapor pressure VOC (LVP-VOC)” means a chemical compound or mixture that contains at least one carbon atom and meets one of the following:\n\n(a) Has a vapor pressure less than 0.1 mm Hg at 20oC, as determined by California Air Resources Board (CARB) Method 310;\n\n(b) Is a chemical compound with more than 12 carbon atoms, or a chemical mixture comprised solely of compounds with more than 12 carbon atoms and the vapor pressure is unknown;\n\n(c) Is a chemical compound with a boiling point greater than 216oC, as determined by CARB Method 310; or\n\n(d) Is the weight percent of a chemical mixture that boils above 216o C, as determined by CARB Method 310.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24 (formerly Env-A 4103.57)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
